    "reviewed_findings": [
      "The final main page and five implementation pages match the five actual trait variants and eleven UI/inventory bindings. Each variant trait ID appears in its matching reverse weapon index; the compatibility table and shared blessing map agree with the actual binding set.",
      "The own-tier proof confirms I–IV attack-side max-hit-mass modifier values .65/.70/.75/.80, percentage formatter prefix +, and five wrappers with one assignment each. The formal tier table and four-level EN/ZH reconstruction match those values and the 5-second common buff duration.",
      "The trigger statement is limited to same-item, held-weapon, positive-damage melee critical events; it does not add kill or stagger requirements. A valid event refreshes one 5-second active window without stacking. Switching weapons suspends the held contribution while the timer continues, and unequipping removes the installed effect.",
      "The direct/special sweep notes preserve the material chainsword distinction: Mk XIIIg direct sweep profiles do not skip on_hit while its four separate sticky follow-up profiles do; Mk IV has only the stated partial sticky-profile exception. The other three implementation pages accurately identify their actual sweep/push-follow-up and special routes.",
      "The first-effect text correctly states that a sweep snapshots max hit mass at start and that the triggering hit/event cannot raise that in-progress sweep limit; a later sweep after event processing and stat-cache update can read the new value.",
      "The formulas distinguish attack-side from impact-side maximum hit mass and use M=max(A,I). Both controlled examples are correct (10×1.65=16.5 with impact 8; 10×1.80=18 while impact 20 remains the selected limit). The write-up does not present the bonus as damage, a target count, or unlimited cleave.",
      "The paired EN/ZH RAW keys and hash match the verification receipt; formatter prefix and tier reconstruction are consistent. The description does not claim unlimited cleave, and omitted runtime conditions are classified as not covered rather than translation errors.",
      "All three icon attachment receipts correspond to the formal image URLs and actual icon IDs 072, 076, and 086; each receipt records public 200/hash/dimension/display verification."
    ],
